<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>KarizmaPlatform.Core</RootNamespace>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <Company>Karizma Stuido</Company>
    <AssemblyVersion>2.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>2.0.0</FileVersion>
    <Version>2.1.0</Version>
    <Authors>Karizma Studio</Authors>
    <Title>Karizma Core</Title>
    <Description>library for EF core Base Classes</Description>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Karizma-Studio/KarizmaCore</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>EFCore, Server, Clean Architecture</RepositoryType>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Version 2.1.0

Added: Unified Service Result &amp; Controller Extension System

Introduced a new ServiceResult&lt;T&gt; class and ResultStatus enum to standardize all service-layer responses.

This change replaces exception-driven flow in controllers with a consistent, type-safe response model.

Added a ControllerExtension helper that maps ServiceResult&lt;T&gt; outcomes to appropriate HTTP responses.

Improved separation of concerns:

The Application layer now returns logical statuses (e.g., Success, Invalid, Unauthorized) instead of HTTP-specific codes.

The Web/API layer maps those statuses to correct HTTP results (e.g., 200 OK, 400 Bad Request, 401 Unauthorized, etc.).

Benefits:

Cleaner, more predictable controller logic

Easier testing and error handling

Reusable service responses across APIs, background jobs, and other integration points</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Core" Version="2.3.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" Version="8.0.10" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.Abstractions" Version="8.0.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="8.0.3" />
  </ItemGroup>



</Project>
